ntion Variants' (e.g., Performers, Linformer) into the LXFL layer to improve cross-modal fusion efficiency without sacrificing performance.\n2. **Hierarchical Reasoning Refinement**: Explore improvements in CHRM by incorporating dynamic attention mechanisms and adaptive processing depths based on task complexity rather than fixed 4-step intervals.\n3. **Contextual Understanding Integration**: Integrate findings from 'Deep Contextual Awareness Models' (e.g., Transformer-XL, Rethink RM) to enhance the model's ability to capture long-range dependencies in language understanding tasks.\n4. **Multimodal Fusion Optimization**: Research alternative fusion strategies like attention-based cross-modal integration or dynamic feature alignment that could potentially overcome limitations of current linear methods.\n5. **Efficiency and Complexity Management**: Continue exploring sub-quadratic implementations (e.g., from 'Linear Transformers' research) to ensure scalability while improving performance across all domains.\n\n**Innovation Direction Guidance**: \n- The primary direction should focus on enhancing the cross-modal fusion layer with more sophisticated attention mechanisms that can handle complex relationships between text and code elements without increasing computational complexity unnecessarily.\n- Secondary innovation involves optimizing hierarchical processing by introducing task-specific adaptive depth controls rather than fixed intervals, which could improve performance efficiency across various cognitive tasks.\n\n**Implementation Strategy**: \n1. **Attention Enhancement Implementation**: Integrate efficient O(n) linear attention variants into the LXFL layer while maintaining its current role in connecting System 1 and System 2 modules.\n2. **Dynamic Processing Depth Control**: Develop mechanisms for adjusting hierarchical reasoning depth based on task complexity, ensuring optimal resource allocation without compromising performance requirements.\n3. **Contextual 