_emb)):\n       # Some operation using rotary_emb[i] and q[:, :, :i]\n   \n   # Fixed code snippet:\n   if pad_len > 0:\n       # Create embeddings with the correct padded sequence length\n       rotary_emb = self.build_rotary_emb(q.shape[2], d_rot, device)\n   ```\n\n4. **Padding Handling Issue**: In `apply_padding`, the original length is not properly tracked when creating new tensors, which can lead to incorrect indexing later on.\n\n   Fixed by: Storing the original length in a separate variable before any padding operations and using that for tensor creation instead of relying on padded dimensions.\n\n   ```python\n   # Original code snippet:\n   o = torch.zeros(q.shape[0], q.shape[1], l, d)  # But l might not be the actual sequence dimension if padded\n   \n   # Fixed code snippet:\n   orig_len = x.shape[2]\n   o = torch.zeros(q.shape[0], q.shape[1], orig_len, d)\n   ```\n\nThese fixes ensure that the architecture remains independent of batch size and can handle varying sequence lengths without breaking. The core logic of attention with rotary embeddings is preserved while making it more robust to different input shapes."}}, "full_result": {"_type": "Dataclass", "_class": "RunResult", "_module": "agents.result", "data": {"input": "Check the implemented code for critical issues and fix them if found.\n\n## Motivation (for context)\nI need to read the current code before writing an improved version.\n\n## YOUR CHECKING TASK\n\nPerform these checks IN ORDER:\n\n### 1. READ AND UNDERSTAND (MANDATORY)\nUse read_code_file to examine the implementation. Understand what the code is trying to achieve based on the motivation.\n\n### 2. STRICT CHECKS - MUST FIX IF FOUND\n\n**A. Mask Correctness Check** 🔴\nExamine all masking operations:\n- Look for attention masks, causal masks, or any position-based masking\n- Verify mask shape matches tensor dimensions\n- Check mask is applied BEFORE softmax or similar operations\n- Ensure mask prevents position i from seeing positions